{"description":"GitHub issue #34: `eka publish --all` lacks explicit draft scope and preflight isolation. It attempts to publish every pending draft in the project unconditionally, mixing unrelated backlogs, and writes partial canonical records when stopped by an unrelated invalid draft.","impact":"Accidental publication of unrelated, work-in-progress drafts. Leaves canonical store in inconsistent state on failure.","acceptanceCriteria":"- Add `--only` or explicit draft scope filter (namespace, tag, ID list) to `eka publish --all`.\n- Implement atomic preflight check for the entire selected set before any writes.\n- Add `--dry-run` flag showing exactly which drafts would be published.\n- If any draft in the batch fails validation, no draft is written (all-or-nothing).\n- Tests covering partial failure rollback and scope filtering."}